From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@thingino.com>
Date: Tue, 08 Sep 2026 00:00:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ingenic-sdk: t41/gc5603 use T41 CIM clock names, not T40's

t41/sensor-src/gc5603.c is a verbatim copy of t40/sensor-src/gc5603.c
and still asks the kernel for T40's numbered CIM clocks (mux_cim0/1/2,
div_cim0/1/2) and T40's epll. Neither exists on T41: clk-t41.c
registers only unnumbered mux_cim/div_cim, and T41 has no epll at all
(only apll/mpll/vpll). clk_get() on the wrong name silently returns
-ENOENT, so sensor->mclk is never obtained, private_clk_set_rate()/
private_clk_prepare_enable() are never reached, and the sensor is left
completely unclocked. With no MCLK the GC5603's own I2C slave logic
never runs, so the chip-ID read at probe NAKs (ret=-EIO, v=0x00) and
sensor_g_chip_ident() reports "is not an gc5603 chip" - read as a
missing/dead sensor, when the real fault is upstream in clock lookup.

Every other T41 sensor driver in this SDK (107 of 108, including the
structurally identical t41/gc5613.c this fix mirrors) already resolves
MCLK via the SEN_MCLK/SEN_BCLK/SEN_TCLK macros from sensor-common.h,
which map to T41's real "mux_cim"/"div_cim"/"vpll" clock names -
gc5603.c is the one file that was never updated when it was ported
from the T40 tree.

Confirmed on real T41LQ+GC5603 hardware (Vanhua T55A board): before
this fix, /proc/jz/clock/clocks shows div_cim parked at its 1104 MHz
reset-time rate with usecount 0 (no driver ever claimed it) and
IMP_ISP_AddSensor fails every 60s. After, div_cim should read 27 MHz
with a non-zero usecount.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@thingino.com>
---
--- a/4.4.94/sensor-src/t41/gc5603.c
+++ b/4.4.94/sensor-src/t41/gc5603.c
@@ -1035,19 +1035,11 @@

 	switch (info->mclk) {
 		case TISP_SENSOR_MCLK0:
-			sclka = private_devm_clk_get(&client->dev, "mux_cim0");
-			sensor->mclk = private_devm_clk_get(sensor->dev, "div_cim0");
-			set_sensor_mclk_function(0);
-			break;
 		case TISP_SENSOR_MCLK1:
-			sclka = private_devm_clk_get(&client->dev, "mux_cim1");
-			sensor->mclk = private_devm_clk_get(sensor->dev, "div_cim1");
-			set_sensor_mclk_function(1);
-			break;
 		case TISP_SENSOR_MCLK2:
-			sclka = private_devm_clk_get(&client->dev, "mux_cim2");
-			sensor->mclk = private_devm_clk_get(sensor->dev, "div_cim2");
-			set_sensor_mclk_function(2);
+			sclka = private_devm_clk_get(&client->dev, SEN_MCLK);
+			sensor->mclk = private_devm_clk_get(sensor->dev, SEN_BCLK);
+			set_sensor_mclk_function(0);
 			break;
 		default:
 			ISP_ERROR("Have no this MCLK Source!!!\n");
@@ -1060,8 +1052,8 @@

 	rate = private_clk_get_rate(sensor->mclk);
 	if (((rate / 1000) % 27000) != 0) {
-		ret = clk_set_parent(sclka, clk_get(NULL, "epll"));
-		sclka = private_devm_clk_get(&client->dev, "epll");
+		ret = clk_set_parent(sclka, clk_get(NULL, SEN_TCLK));
+		sclka = private_devm_clk_get(&client->dev, SEN_TCLK);
 		if (IS_ERR(sclka)) {
 			pr_err("get sclka failed\n");
 		} else {
